If you haven't received the Gauntlets of Defense yet, sacrifice until
you get them.  They give half damage, toggle invisibility, and improve
your AC quite a bit due to Slashem's high dexterity AC bonus.

Since you have Pw regen, going around as a crystal golem is very
tempting - you will be able to cast your breath weapon freely.  You
don't even need HP regeneration or unchanging, since you can bring your
HP back up to 300 by rehumanizing and re-golemizing.

You will probably want to put the Eye on to give yourself telepathy
until you aquire it again.  Even if it is cursed, it doesn't matter
much - a little sacrificing and your god will uncurse it even if you
don't pray.

If you go around as a crystal golem (wearing the GoDef) all the time,
you will be immune to almost everything.  There are still a few things
to be concerned about, but you should be able to handle them.

1) Starving
2) getting digested
3) Green slime
4) Sickness
5) Lava

You will not have to worry about drowning, choking, stoning, fire,
cold, disintegration, or most other dangers.  But you should still play
carefully, and be ready to escape if something starts kicking your ass.
 Remember you can invoke the Eye to levelport even on non-teleport
levels, as long as you aren't carrying the Amulet of Yendor.

When you are ready to face Master Kaen, I would recommend entering the
final quest level as a crystal golem, immediately reading a scroll of
earth (while standing on the up-stairs), then engraving Elbereth with a
wand of fire or lightning.  You can use your breath weapon on MK from
behind your boulder fort without anyone attacking you.  Eventually you
will surely destroy him.

By the way - in Slashem you don't need holy water to bless things.  You
can also get things blessed by
1) Wield them while sacrificing.  Small but useful chance.
2) Hallucinate while requesting a shopkeeper uncurse.  You can eat
yellow or violet molds to induce hallucination.  The odds of getting
the item blessed are 1/4, so this will require some credit.  Remember,
in Slashem hallucination also prevents you from seeing your inventory,
so you will need to keep the inventory letters of the items you want
blessed and your unicorn horn where you won't forget them.


